WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:03.260
<i>I'm Natsuko Hirose.</i>

00:03.260 --> 00:06.160
<i>After graduating high school, 
I became an animator,</i>

00:06.160 --> 00:08.580
<i>honed my craft as much as I could,</i>

00:08.580 --> 00:11.230
<i>then made my debut as a director.</i>

00:10.610 --> 00:11.820
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

00:10.610 --> 00:11.820
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

00:10.610 --> 00:11.820
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

00:10.900 --> 00:11.820
Director: Natsuko Hirose

00:11.820 --> 00:14.530
<b>Opening Next Spring</b>

00:11.820 --> 00:14.530
<b>Today Is Yesterday,\h\h
Tomorrow Is Now,\h\h
And Every Day Is Summer.</b>

00:11.820 --> 00:14.530
<b>Director / Natsuko Hirose</b>

00:11.820 --> 00:14.910
<i>My next work is an original 
rom-com feature film.</i>

00:13.820 --> 00:15.240
<b>HATSUKOI:
First Love</b>

00:14.910 --> 00:17.200
<i>Another masterpiece is born.</i>

00:15.240 --> 00:15.740
<b>HATSUKOI:
First Love</b>

00:15.740 --> 00:16.620
<b>HATSUKOI:
First Love</b>

00:16.620 --> 00:16.950
<b>HATSUKOI:
First Love</b>

00:16.950 --> 00:17.210
<b>HATSUKOI:
First Love</b>

00:18.070 --> 00:20.240
<i>Or it should've been.</i>

00:20.240 --> 00:22.700
<i>However, I ate a rotten clam lunch and died.</i>

00:22.080 --> 00:24.450
Natsuko!

00:24.450 --> 00:28.750
<i>Somehow, I ended up being reborn in 
the world of the movie, </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>.</i>

00:28.750 --> 00:30.680
<i>Blah, blah, yada, yada.</i>

00:31.700 --> 00:33.090
<i>A lot happened.</i>

00:36.620 --> 00:46.010
Natsuko! Natsuko! Natsuko! Natsuko!

00:39.980 --> 00:42.580
<i>And I ended up becoming
one of the Nine Soldiers.</i>

02:16.490 --> 02:20.950
Episode 3: DESTINY

02:19.560 --> 02:21.230
Sorry to keep you waiting.

02:22.120 --> 02:25.840
Memmeln! You look amazing in that dress!

02:25.840 --> 02:29.130
Why do I have to dress like this?

02:29.520 --> 02:32.380
I can barely breathe, 
and it's so hard to walk.

02:33.080 --> 02:34.380
Wow.

02:34.380 --> 02:35.800
What're you starin' at?

02:35.800 --> 02:39.500
You look nice. This is way better than 
those weird clothes you usually wear.

02:39.500 --> 02:41.450
You look like a lovely uggo.

02:41.990 --> 02:44.600
And you look better 
than your usual naked self.

02:44.600 --> 02:46.610
Like a pack mule owned by some rich guy.

02:46.610 --> 02:48.190
Who're you calling a pack mule?!

02:49.500 --> 02:51.680
Everyone in the town is watching you.

02:52.300 --> 02:55.830
<i>Oh, right. In the movie, </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>,</i>

02:56.280 --> 03:00.450
<i>the town almost gets completely 
wiped out by the Voids from the sky.</i>

03:01.580 --> 03:04.160
<i>And there's supposed to be a joint funeral</i>

03:04.160 --> 03:08.410
<i>for the victims and Unio, who died in battle
 using a spell to blow himself up, but...</i>

03:09.070 --> 03:12.580
We will now begin the harvest festival!

03:15.210 --> 03:17.340
<i>It all somehow ended up as a festival.</i>

03:17.640 --> 03:19.810
Priest, if you would.

03:35.850 --> 03:37.360
Ga-go!

03:37.630 --> 03:39.350
Ga-go!

03:39.580 --> 03:40.610
What is this?

03:39.950 --> 03:41.520
Ga-go!

03:40.610 --> 03:43.810
It's a ritual to give thanks 
to the Soul Future.

03:42.120 --> 03:43.560
Ga-go!

03:43.810 --> 03:45.610
Don't you need to participate?

03:43.970 --> 03:45.640
Ga-go!

03:45.610 --> 03:50.300
Well, this ritual only started
 about 200 years ago.

03:45.890 --> 03:47.320
Ga-go!

03:50.300 --> 03:53.410
I don't have much interest in passing fads.

03:53.410 --> 03:54.390
Oh, I see.

04:07.110 --> 04:08.390
Yeah!

04:08.390 --> 04:11.270
This is so fun!

04:11.270 --> 04:13.130
All right, let's go.

04:13.130 --> 04:14.020
Wha—

04:14.020 --> 04:16.140
We need to prepare for the next battle.

04:16.140 --> 04:17.760
But it's the harvest festival!

04:17.760 --> 04:20.620
It's the day we give thanks 
to the Soul Future and have fun.

04:20.620 --> 04:22.890
Come on, Luke. Have some wine.

04:22.890 --> 04:26.010
No. We don't know when 
the Voids will attack next.

04:26.010 --> 04:27.200
Aw, come on.

04:28.270 --> 04:32.580
I'm pretty sure the next time 
the Voids show up is on a rainy day.

04:32.580 --> 04:33.670
What?

04:33.990 --> 04:34.790
Rain?

04:34.790 --> 04:36.830
QJ, what's the probability of rain?

04:37.150 --> 04:41.580
Beepity beep. The current chance of rain is 0%.

04:41.580 --> 04:45.290
It will likely be next month 
before it rains again in the Last Town.

04:45.290 --> 04:47.830
See? I think we'll be okay for one day.

04:47.830 --> 04:49.250
Don't be so careless.

04:49.250 --> 04:53.840
Natsuko's predictions <i>have</i> been 
pretty spot on. You said so yourself, Luke.

04:53.840 --> 04:57.490
We're the Nine Soldiers. We have to 
be prepared to fight at any moment!

04:57.490 --> 04:58.930
Great hero!

04:59.310 --> 05:01.950
Wow! It <i>is</i> the great hero!

05:01.950 --> 05:04.180
May we come and chat with you?

05:04.180 --> 05:05.160
Go right ahead.

05:05.160 --> 05:08.900
What? No, wait! Unio...

05:05.640 --> 05:07.460
Great hero, what are your hobbies?

05:07.460 --> 05:11.460
Great hero, will you dance with me?

05:08.900 --> 05:10.830
No, wait.

05:09.910 --> 05:11.460
What's your favorite food?

05:11.460 --> 05:13.020
Have fun!

05:11.620 --> 05:13.220
Unio! Unio!

05:13.020 --> 05:15.480
I guess heroes are super popular.

05:19.500 --> 05:21.160
Unicorns are also...

05:21.690 --> 05:23.320
pretty popular, too.

05:29.070 --> 05:32.530
Would you ladies like to ride on my back?

05:35.280 --> 05:36.630
Good day.

05:36.630 --> 05:40.170
Memmeln, the choir is gathering over there.

05:40.170 --> 05:42.040
We'd love for you to join us.

05:42.040 --> 05:43.960
Yes, of course.

05:45.010 --> 05:46.360
Choir?

05:46.360 --> 05:52.410
Memmeln and the other choir members use 
the power of song to heal the souls of the dead.

05:59.170 --> 06:02.940
<i>There are no deadlines and no other 
responsibilities looming over me.</i>

06:04.370 --> 06:07.440
It's been so long since 
I've spent time like this.

06:12.560 --> 06:15.870
Which one, which one should 
I ask to ride on my back?

06:15.870 --> 06:17.950
Hey. Let's leave already.

06:17.950 --> 06:21.320
You're joking, right? You're totally 
having a blast being so popular.

06:21.320 --> 06:22.770
I am <i>not</i>!

06:24.660 --> 06:26.790
Well, I love it!

06:30.450 --> 06:32.930
I've got meat and other yummies!

06:33.470 --> 06:35.120
Enjoying yourself?

06:35.120 --> 06:37.980
Oh, Elder Baobab! Would you like some?

06:37.980 --> 06:39.450
No, that's quite all right.

06:40.430 --> 06:44.030
How are you able to see into the future?

06:44.030 --> 06:48.790
I've explained this before, 
but this is a world in an anime, and...

06:49.450 --> 06:51.960
I've seen this movie 
an insane number of times.

06:51.960 --> 06:54.360
Is it similar to having prophetic dreams?

06:54.360 --> 06:56.100
Um, sure. Let's go with that.

06:58.600 --> 07:01.090
According to my ancient texts,

07:01.330 --> 07:05.100
if all of the Soul Futures 
are eaten by the Voids,

07:05.100 --> 07:09.480
the Ultimate Void will appear
and the world will end.

07:09.710 --> 07:15.880
The Nine Soldiers will stop that from happening,
 save this world, and become the true light.

07:16.210 --> 07:19.460
What does the future you see hold for us?

07:27.960 --> 07:30.360
Well, today is the harvest festival.

07:30.760 --> 07:34.500
Let us converse on this matter another time.

07:36.510 --> 07:39.760
Great hero! Where did you go?

07:40.070 --> 07:41.400
Luke?

07:40.330 --> 07:42.050
Great hero!

07:43.400 --> 07:44.820
<i>Hey, wait.</i>

07:44.820 --> 07:49.160
<i>If this goes like the movie, this is 
after Unio's funeral, which means...</i>

07:49.160 --> 07:50.950
<i></i>she's<i> going to appear.</i>

07:51.280 --> 07:52.900
Great hero!

07:54.290 --> 07:55.700
Oh, I'm so sorry!

07:55.700 --> 07:57.740
<i>And there she is!</i>

07:59.400 --> 08:00.290
Are you all right?

08:00.590 --> 08:03.500
I'm sorry. I spilled my drink on you.

08:03.500 --> 08:05.030
Destiny!

08:05.030 --> 08:07.160
Des-ti-ny!

08:08.790 --> 08:12.050
Oh, where did you go, my love?

08:12.050 --> 08:13.260
I'm so sorry!

08:14.230 --> 08:16.000
Destiny!

08:16.000 --> 08:18.550
Hm. Destiny!

08:19.660 --> 08:21.410
Who are they?

08:21.410 --> 08:24.420
Oh, you've got some alcohol on your face.

08:25.440 --> 08:27.600
Ah! I'm so sorry!

08:28.820 --> 08:30.240
Destiny.

08:31.240 --> 08:33.740
Have a wonderful time 
at the harvest festival.

08:34.170 --> 08:36.750
Destiny Heartwarming.

08:37.170 --> 08:40.620
<i>The daughter of the mayor,
 Destiny lives a sheltered life,</i>

08:40.620 --> 08:45.240
<i>knowing nothing of the world, and not 
realizing Luke is one of the Nine Soldiers.</i>

08:45.240 --> 08:49.740
<i>Originally, Destiny was destined 
to meet Luke at Unio's funeral.</i>

08:49.740 --> 08:53.750
<i>Destiny was destined to always 
show up in places she didn't belong.</i>

08:53.750 --> 08:57.390
<i>The root cause of all 
their troubles is always...</i>

08:57.390 --> 09:00.640
Destiny!

09:00.640 --> 09:04.230
Are you really, <i>really</i> 
going to marry the chairman?

09:04.230 --> 09:05.390
Daddy.

09:05.690 --> 09:11.900
He promised he would build
 an orphanage in this town.

09:11.900 --> 09:15.200
It's for the sake of 
the children of this town.

09:15.200 --> 09:20.380
The chairman's rich, so he should be 
able to give you whatever you want,

09:20.380 --> 09:22.790
but Daddy's gonna miss you!

09:22.790 --> 09:23.340
Mayor.

09:23.340 --> 09:24.050
Luke?

09:25.010 --> 09:27.470
Are you enjoying the harvest festival?

09:27.470 --> 09:28.310
Um, well...

09:28.310 --> 09:33.500
Destiny, allow me to introduce the hero
 of the Nine Soldiers, Luke Braveheart.

09:33.500 --> 09:34.340
What?

09:34.340 --> 09:35.830
You're the...

09:35.830 --> 09:38.220
And this is my daughter, Destiny.

09:38.650 --> 09:40.300
Destiny?

09:42.960 --> 09:44.360
Mhm.

09:47.840 --> 09:49.780
S-So bright!

09:49.780 --> 09:53.610
No wonder she's the heroine.
Her radiance is on a whole other level!

09:53.610 --> 09:57.740
Luke, she's a total cutie. 
You little weasel.

09:57.740 --> 09:58.810
Mayor!

09:59.170 --> 10:02.100
We'd like for you to check 
the harvest fireworks.

10:02.100 --> 10:03.500
Yes, very well.

10:03.500 --> 10:05.510
If you'll excuse me.

10:05.510 --> 10:07.840
Well, hello there!

10:06.560 --> 10:07.900
H-Hey!

10:07.840 --> 10:12.630
I'd love to let you ride on my back, 
but you'll have to settle for Luke.

10:12.630 --> 10:15.500
You young'uns enjoy yourselves!

10:27.880 --> 10:29.150
<i>And Luke...</i>

10:31.540 --> 10:33.850
<i>falls in love with Destiny.</i>

10:35.050 --> 10:38.410
"She's beautiful, rich, 
and has a gentle heart."

10:38.410 --> 10:40.680
"She has everything I don't."

10:40.680 --> 10:43.170
"Oh, how loathsome! How I loathe that woman!"

10:43.170 --> 10:48.030
Hey, could you <i>not</i> narrate my inner monologue
unsolicited? Not that I'm thinking any of that.

10:48.030 --> 10:51.360
Luke needs all the fun he can get.

10:52.430 --> 10:55.800
Ever since he was born, 
he's been the legendary hero,

10:56.090 --> 10:58.720
and all he's ever done is fight.

10:59.130 --> 11:00.360
I know.

11:02.360 --> 11:05.780
<i>The only one who could make Luke 
smile from the bottom of his heart...</i>

11:06.350 --> 11:08.050
<i>was Destiny.</i>

11:10.370 --> 11:11.350
<i>So...</i>

11:38.120 --> 11:39.410
Right this way.

11:41.430 --> 11:46.060
Oh, hello, Great Priest!

11:46.060 --> 11:47.150
Huh?

11:47.500 --> 11:50.360
Wait, there are <i>two</i> priests?

11:50.360 --> 11:54.190
Maybe we drank too much.

11:54.560 --> 11:57.340
Man, this feels so much better!

11:57.340 --> 11:59.350
All right! Back to eating!

12:00.820 --> 12:01.950
Oh?

12:01.950 --> 12:04.520
Destiny! Where's Luke?

12:04.520 --> 12:06.950
Actually, we got separated.

12:07.480 --> 12:08.860
Who's this bearded person?

12:08.860 --> 12:11.160
This is the "anneemator," Natsuko Hirose.

12:11.160 --> 12:13.390
What? You're Natsuko?

12:13.390 --> 12:16.790
Daddy told me there was 
a person with amazing powers,

12:16.790 --> 12:19.030
but I had no idea you were so cute!

12:19.030 --> 12:24.690
As if! This black-haired gremlin eats 
a stupid amount of food, and she's violent—

12:25.040 --> 12:27.510
My bad for being so violent!

12:31.600 --> 12:34.340
Man, your personality sucks!

12:34.340 --> 12:36.160
I bet you don't have any friends!

12:36.160 --> 12:36.980
What?

12:37.520 --> 12:40.780
Natsuko, you don't have any friends?

12:41.170 --> 12:42.320
Not really.

12:42.320 --> 12:47.600
Really? None at all? Not even one?

12:47.600 --> 12:50.560
It's not like I need any. 
I can survive just fine without any.

12:52.130 --> 12:56.300
I don't have any either! We're so alike.

12:58.530 --> 13:00.410
Destiny!

13:02.410 --> 13:03.220
Destiny.

13:03.700 --> 13:06.760
I'm overjoyed that you've
 accepted my proposal.

13:11.030 --> 13:13.970
Destiny's engaged to the chairman?

13:14.670 --> 13:18.740
<i>He's the chairman of the foundation 
that's the source of funds for the Last Town.</i>

13:18.740 --> 13:21.110
<i>He has eight wives.</i>

13:21.380 --> 13:25.000
You will be my ninth wife. Wife number nine.

13:25.000 --> 13:28.750
Hm, first, we'll have to do 
something about your clothes

13:28.750 --> 13:31.620
and your hair to make you 
look more like you're my wife.

13:31.620 --> 13:32.970
Oh, okay.

13:32.970 --> 13:33.960
Why?

13:33.960 --> 13:34.610
Huh?

13:34.900 --> 13:36.570
Why are you marrying him?

13:36.570 --> 13:39.110
And what is this talking clump of hair?

13:39.110 --> 13:42.380
Ever since I was a kid, 
I've never understood it.

13:42.670 --> 13:46.130
Your dream is to have an orphanage 
built in the Last Town, right?

13:46.130 --> 13:48.340
Then, why not build one yourself?

13:49.480 --> 13:51.580
Oh, what's this?

13:51.580 --> 13:55.170
Destiny is destined to be my wife.
 Are you jealous?

13:55.170 --> 13:55.970
Huh?

13:55.970 --> 13:58.730
Your strange attire and your hair.

13:58.730 --> 14:00.970
Definitely not my type.

14:00.970 --> 14:06.240
If you want to be wife number nine, 
you'll have to become like my other wives.

14:06.240 --> 14:09.610
Beautiful!

14:09.610 --> 14:13.000
Beautiful!

14:13.000 --> 14:15.760
I'll dress how I want and live how I want.

14:18.660 --> 14:20.300
That's <i>my</i> definition of...

14:22.590 --> 14:23.830
beautiful.

14:26.380 --> 14:28.510
Th-Th-Th-There's trouble!

14:28.510 --> 14:31.250
Void response detected! There's a Void here!

14:31.250 --> 14:32.010
What?!

14:32.010 --> 14:32.960
Here?!

14:32.960 --> 14:37.140
I'm sorry! It must have snuck in
 while I was recharging!

14:37.140 --> 14:38.410
You piece of junk!

14:38.410 --> 14:41.010
Wait, I thought no Voids 
were supposed to appear!

14:42.230 --> 14:43.350
Where is it?

14:43.590 --> 14:44.520
Hm?

14:44.520 --> 14:47.270
There are two priests?

14:49.770 --> 14:52.350
What? What's going on here?

14:52.350 --> 14:54.010
The Void is close by!

14:54.600 --> 14:55.830
That means...

14:55.830 --> 14:57.310
One of the priests is the Void!

14:57.310 --> 14:59.500
H-Huh? What did you just say?!

14:59.500 --> 15:01.950
Wh-What do you mean by that, Natsuko?

15:01.950 --> 15:03.680
That's what happens in the movie.

15:03.680 --> 15:07.020
Hey now! <i>You</i> said they 
wouldn't show up today!

15:07.020 --> 15:08.300
I mean...

15:08.680 --> 15:13.060
The part where a Void sneaks into the town 
disguised as the priest happens much later...

15:13.420 --> 15:15.430
What're we gonna do about this?

15:15.970 --> 15:18.430
They are too similar for me
 to tell which is which.

15:18.430 --> 15:21.450
The way to find the Void is...

15:23.930 --> 15:24.890
Huh?

15:24.890 --> 15:26.390
If you're a Void...

15:26.390 --> 15:27.920
Look! Can you do this?

15:27.920 --> 15:31.420
There's no <i>way</i> a Void could do
 this delightfully fun move!

15:31.420 --> 15:33.900
You are seriously out of your mind.

15:38.380 --> 15:39.880
That's the Void!

15:39.880 --> 15:40.470
Huh?

15:47.950 --> 15:50.100
I can't believe the Void camouflaged itself!

15:52.600 --> 15:55.280
Everyone, take shelter! Hurry!

15:57.180 --> 16:00.940
What? Hurry, my wives. Beautiful!

16:00.940 --> 16:03.630
I've never seen a Void like that before!

16:04.750 --> 16:06.570
What should we do, Luke?

16:09.100 --> 16:09.820
Huh?

16:10.990 --> 16:12.560
This is vodka!

16:12.810 --> 16:15.580
Destiny, why'd you get him to drink <i>that</i>?

16:15.580 --> 16:21.120
<i>The root cause of all their
 troubles is always Destiny.</i>

16:25.080 --> 16:27.510
Please escape below. You'll be all right.

16:27.510 --> 16:28.670
Thank you.

16:28.670 --> 16:30.620
Thank you, miss.

16:32.820 --> 16:34.330
I need to get the others—

16:34.850 --> 16:37.280
Huh? What?

16:46.720 --> 16:47.990
Destiny!

16:49.930 --> 16:52.350
My eyes... and body...

16:57.350 --> 16:58.360
Luke!

16:59.470 --> 17:02.110
Draw. You need to draw, Natsuko.

17:02.840 --> 17:06.280
Look, I've been meaning to say this, 
but could you make it sound less like an order?

17:06.280 --> 17:07.050
Draw!

17:07.050 --> 17:08.370
Okay, okay, I get it.

17:08.370 --> 17:11.120
Uh, what should I draw at a time like this?

17:11.770 --> 17:13.380
Amideki— Whoa!

17:17.270 --> 17:18.400
That's it!

17:50.540 --> 17:51.630
All right!

17:59.390 --> 18:01.730
Natsuko, hurry!

18:06.800 --> 18:10.660
Natsuko! Are you almost done?
 I'm reaching my limit!

18:10.660 --> 18:11.730
Almost done.

18:18.770 --> 18:19.860
Done!

18:22.140 --> 18:25.470
Go! Serval Cat Mask!

18:38.850 --> 18:44.300
And now, the battle for the Soul Future that
 will determine the fate of the world begins.

18:44.300 --> 18:48.010
It's our beloved Serval Cat Mask 
versus the evil Praying Mantis Void.

18:48.010 --> 18:52.030
Both are ready to fight.
 They inch closer and closer.

18:52.380 --> 18:53.810
And here they go!

18:54.330 --> 18:56.000
Just look at those fierce blows!

18:56.000 --> 18:58.060
Who's going to come out on top?

18:59.050 --> 19:01.660
Serval Cat grabs his opponent!

19:02.970 --> 19:05.620
It's a Lightning Cat Fight Savate!

19:05.620 --> 19:09.830
Next, he slams into this evil incarnate
 with a Mongolian Chop!

19:10.750 --> 19:13.020
Th-That's so cool!

19:13.020 --> 19:15.960
You've got this, Serval Cat Mask!

19:15.960 --> 19:18.390
You can do it!

19:18.390 --> 19:21.550
You can do it! You can do it!

19:19.390 --> 19:20.510
What the...

19:22.060 --> 19:26.670
This move's definitely high in 
animation calories: the Dragon Suplex!

19:26.670 --> 19:28.060
Go!

19:34.560 --> 19:36.560
He's so cool!

19:39.230 --> 19:40.840
He leaps off the corner post!

19:41.660 --> 19:45.570
The Praying Mantis Void reveals its evil face
 as a final show of resistance.

19:45.570 --> 19:48.170
This special move took 
three days' worth of drawing.

19:48.170 --> 19:51.280
The Raging Explosion Void Bomber!

19:53.540 --> 19:55.920
And we start the countdown to victory!

19:55.920 --> 19:56.550
One!

19:56.550 --> 19:57.550
Two!

19:57.550 --> 19:58.510
Three!

20:00.840 --> 20:03.890
All right!

20:08.340 --> 20:10.860
Wow! That was so amazing!

20:10.860 --> 20:14.310
Thank you, Serval Cat Mask!

20:17.120 --> 20:19.750
Great job... guys...

20:19.750 --> 20:20.860
Natsuko?

20:22.250 --> 20:24.670
I-Is she okay?

20:24.670 --> 20:26.880
Yes. She's just asleep.

20:29.760 --> 20:32.090
Mm, this is so good.

20:32.090 --> 20:33.880
You slept for three days again.

20:33.880 --> 20:36.900
Guess I sleep off the amount 
of calories the animation costs.

20:38.130 --> 20:40.330
That would've taken me 
about three days to draw.

20:40.640 --> 20:43.060
I guess I should thank you.

20:43.060 --> 20:45.600
Thank you for protecting the town.

20:45.600 --> 20:47.080
I'm seriously unmatched.

20:47.470 --> 20:51.360
Also, why's my hair tied up in 
such a weird way whenever I wake up?

20:53.230 --> 20:54.490
Nacchan.

20:57.350 --> 21:00.020
Thank goodness. You're awake.

21:00.020 --> 21:01.230
Who's that?

21:01.230 --> 21:02.290
It's Destiny.

21:02.290 --> 21:02.930
What?

21:02.930 --> 21:06.350
You see, I turned down 
the chairman's proposal,

21:06.350 --> 21:09.110
and decided to start an orphanage myself!

21:09.110 --> 21:11.860
I'll do my best, 
so I hope you'll support me.

21:12.380 --> 21:14.100
Yeah, sure.

21:14.100 --> 21:16.580
So why are you wearing that weird mask?

21:16.580 --> 21:21.390
Serval Cat Mask was just so cool!

21:21.390 --> 21:24.000
I want to be as strong as him!

21:25.310 --> 21:28.850
I'll dress how I want and live how I want.

21:31.570 --> 21:33.050
Hey, Memmeln.

21:33.050 --> 21:35.190
Do you wanna ride on my back?

21:35.190 --> 21:36.260
Absolutely not.

21:36.890 --> 21:38.810
Destiny-chwan!

21:38.810 --> 21:41.010
Aw, you're wearing that mask again?

21:41.010 --> 21:44.460
But I wanna see your adorable face.

21:45.120 --> 21:48.500
By the way, Memmeln, 
where were you during the festival?

21:49.250 --> 21:51.800
I mean, you weren't around 
when the Void showed up.

21:52.260 --> 21:53.250
Indeed.

21:53.250 --> 21:57.430
Well, you see, Memmeln was busy with the choir.

21:57.430 --> 22:00.290
Unlike you, she actually has friends!

21:58.610 --> 22:01.280
Serval Destiny Chop!

22:02.140 --> 22:06.480
I won't let anyone talk badly
 about my friends!

22:04.310 --> 22:06.480
You go, Serval Destiny!

23:49.990 --> 23:54.900
<b>Episode 4: "ETERNITY"</b>
